# "(" is a different token in different lexer states (popen after a
# pattern operator, lparen elsewhere). The grammar uses both, so the
# token an `X "("` hint names is ambiguous: a located error naming both
# terminals, never the first rule's token.
# error: x_hint_ambiguous_token.grammar:27:10:
# error: X "(" on expr → IDENT is ambiguous: lexer rules make that text POPEN or LPAREN
@lexer
state
    pat = 0
tokens
    ident
    lparen
    popen
    rparen
    query
    eof
    err
'\n'                                        → skip, skip
'(' @ pat                                   → popen, {pat = 0}
'('                                         → lparen
')'                                         → rparen
'?'                                         → query, {pat = 1}
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
exprs! = expr+                              → (exprs ...1)
expr   = IDENT X "("                        → (var 1)
       | IDENT LPAREN expr RPAREN           → (call 1 3)
       | LPAREN expr RPAREN                 → 2
       | QUERY POPEN expr RPAREN            → (pat 3)
